  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The first conjugation",
     "texto": [
      "Many regular, common verbs end in **-ать** in the infinitive: **делать** (to do), **работать** (to work), **читать** (to read).",
      "In regular verbs of this pattern, **-ть** is removed and these endings are added: **-ю, -ешь, -ет, -ем, -ете, -ют**.",
      "The first conjugation also has **-у/-ут** variants, like **живу/живут**; some verbs change the root.",
      "In Russian, the subject pronoun is usually said, as in English. In the third person singular, **он**, **она** and **оно** use the same verb form: **делает**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "«Делать» and «работать»",
     "columnas": [
