    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "More verbs that conjugate the same way",
     "texto": [
      "They conjugate in the same way: **читать** (to read), **слушать** (to listen), **гулять** (to go for a walk), **отдыхать** (to rest), and the three meals: **завтракать** (to have breakfast), **обедать** (to have lunch) and **ужинать** (to have dinner).",
      "**Что ты делаешь?** = what are you doing? For the formal singular or for several people: **Что вы делаете?**"
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "When",
     "texto": [
      "Parts of the day are said with a single word: **утром** (in the morning), **днём** (during the day, at midday), **вечером** (in the afternoon) and **ночью** (at night).",
      "**Сейчас** = now. **Потом** = after that.",
      "The Russian present is used for habits and actions in progress: **Я сейчас работаю** can mean «I work now» or «I am working now», depending on the context.",
      "A preview of the accusative: many feminine nouns ending in **-а** change to **-у** as the direct object: книга → читаю **книгу**, музыка → слушаю **музыку**. You will study this calmly in the next chapter."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
